{
 "what": "The 24x24 upper Hessenberg that Arnoldi builds for the Faraday monodromy map, and on which shifted QR without a closed-form 2x2 deflation does not converge. Its dominant two eigenvalues are the Floquet multipliers, coalesced into a near-defective pair: LAPACK splits them as -1.6495911901867406 and -1.6495911749758638, 1.5e-8 apart, which is sqrt(eps) and is all a defective pair admits. The trailing 2x2 the iteration is left with has a subdiagonal that floors at 2.8e-9 to 7.0e-9 and oscillates with period two, so the 1e-16 relative deflation test is never satisfied and the iteration runs to its cap. Committed as a fixture because no small synthetic matrix reproduces it -- see the search recorded in check 12(a) of check-dns.mjs.",
